        "body": "Start with a stable customer and invoice identifier. Record invoice number, issue date, due date shown, currency, billed amount, open balance, ledger status, purchase-order reference, account owner, and source links. Preserve the current ledger state before anyone makes an adjustment. Separate a customer-stated balance from the accounting record. If the customer says only half is owed, record that as the disputed position. Do not overwrite the open balance to make the packet match the email. Use read-only access during preparation where possible. The assistant does not need payment-release, journal-entry, credit-memo, or bank-edit permission to collect evidence."
